template.comment.schedule.backup_player_:
# Backup player gate: when online players reach this count, scheduled backups are postponed until the count drops below it;
# while a backup is running, players staying above the threshold for backup_player_gate_overlimit_seconds interrupt the backup and restore world autosave.
# This threshold is the gate's only switch: above 0 enables it, 0 disables it. All new configs start at 5:
# remote repositories (sftp/rest/s3/rclone etc.) upload slowly and keep save-off active until the backup finishes, which can exhaust server memory at peak;
# local repositories may set it to 0 if backups are fast and the risk is understood. Changing a non-zero value to 0 means you consciously accept the risk.

